# Rust
/target
/.build-temp/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Avoid accidentally adding additional original game data
# Keep these exact original-data names out of Git.  Do not use broad
# case-insensitive patterns here: on Windows `RESOURCE.*` also ignores the
# Rust module `crates/wilson-dgds/src/resource.rs`.
/RESOURCE.MAP
/RESOURCE.001
/RESOURCE.00$
# The original Windows 3.1 reference binary is retained separately.
/SCRANTIC.SC$
data/
# The release-package placeholder is documentation, not game data.
!/packaging/
!/packaging/windows/
!/packaging/windows/data/
!/packaging/windows/data/PUT-ORIGINAL-FILES-HERE.txt
assets-original/
# This repository deliberately includes the reference test resource set so
# the Castaway_Screensaver v1.0.0 embedded Windows build is reproducible.
!/test-original-data/
releases/*.exe
# Reference implementations (third-party) are kept only locally, never committed —
# clone the upstreams yourself (see docs/knowledge-base/06-projetos-de-referencia.md).
# dist.zip (the encrypted test bundle) is copyrighted game data — never commit it.
/repos/
/dist.zip

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
